WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.280
Think about this: What should an AI case
brief do with a disputed

00:00:04.280 --> 00:00:06.620
entitlement? Let’s work through it
together.

00:00:07.240 --> 00:00:12.180
I'm Doctor Gainz. Lesson 18: Coordinate
with the appropriate professional.

00:00:12.960 --> 00:00:16.180
Some situations require legal judgment or
representation.

00:00:16.840 --> 00:00:22.300
Examples include disputed entitlement,
estates, entities, competing claims,

00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:25.720
assignments, and questions about permitted
compensation.

00:00:25.720 --> 00:00:30.800
Requirements vary. A professional handoff
should ask a focused question

00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:34.900
instead of asking someone to validate a
conclusion an AI already announced

00:00:34.900 --> 00:00:39.780
to the client. Explain who performs each
task, who communicates with the

00:00:39.780 --> 00:00:44.480
custodian, who may sign or file, and how
costs are handled under reviewed

00:00:44.480 --> 00:00:49.180
terms. Obtain appropriate permission
before sharing client information.

00:00:49.780 --> 00:00:53.640
Do not promise that a professional will
accept a case, that a fee will be

00:00:53.640 --> 00:00:57.160
allowed, or that a referral arrangement is
lawful without review.

00:00:57.860 --> 00:00:59.860
Keep a written responsibility list.

00:01:00.400 --> 00:01:04.300
A helpful administrative role can coexist
with professional representation,

00:01:04.680 --> 00:01:06.520
but boundaries must be explicit.

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:11.080
When a professional requests
clarification, update the evidence file
and

00:01:11.080 --> 00:01:15.020
retain the earlier version rather than
silently changing what was supplied.

00:01:15.820 --> 00:01:17.000
Pause and try this.

00:01:17.600 --> 00:01:21.820
Draft a fictional handoff request asking
about a disputed interest and the

00:01:21.820 --> 00:01:23.560
limits of administrative assistance.

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:26.080
Include no private person’s information.

00:01:26.900 --> 00:01:31.200
Quick knowledge check. What should an AI
case brief do with a disputed

00:01:31.200 --> 00:01:35.920
entitlement? The answer: Flag the sourced
dispute for the appropriate

00:01:35.920 --> 00:01:41.040
review. A case brief supports review; it
does not exercise legal authority.

00:01:41.660 --> 00:01:44.560
Keep the source, the date, and the
unknowns visible.

00:01:45.200 --> 00:01:46.380
I'll see you in the next lesson.
